<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bethel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bethel was an ancient town north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, usually identified with Beitin in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a>. The Bible links it with Abraham and Jacob, and after the division of the kingdom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeroboam-i">Jeroboam I</a> set up a royal shrine there with a golden calf to rival Jerusalem. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah">Josiah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> is said to have destroyed its altar in the late 7th century BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bethel.jpg" alt="Bethel" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francis Frith · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bethel_MET_DP116361.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
